    "created_at": "2025-12-12T17:01:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-12T17:01:43Z",
    "body": "Giving an update here: Unless we've made a mistake, this issue causes quite major webcompat issues on reddit. Double-clicking posts makes the URL and page go out of sync. We are currently landing [a fix](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2005771) for this, which deliberately breaks the `window.stop()` case above.\n\nI'm curious though how this can work in Chrome and Safari. ",
